{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult","id":1216863,"title":"The Unconventional Cult","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-08T17:18:12-07:00","id":1216863,"title":"The Unconventional Cult","content":"I like that M20 calls a &quot;sanctum&quot; a &quot;lab&quot;, an &quot;avatar&quot; &quot;genius&quot; and so on. Alternative names for Backgrounds are neat and help to reinforce the divisions between different paradigms, while reinforcing satirical elements; everyone is doing the same thing differently.<br /> <br /> However, Cult is presented in a pretty by-the-numbers way. It's just a cult of adherents who believe in your teachings and help with rituals, when the cult is gathered. No surprising examples. Sanctums? They're mystic grottos, dark basements filled with tomes, attics filled with old machines, cutting edge labs, dojos, new age meditation spaces... Cults? They're just... cults.<br /> <br /> Personally I would keep the mechanics, but reframe the concept. All the Cult background does is give you a group of people who support you to a fault (ranging from ordinary and unremarkable Sleepers, whose devotion and limited ability is purchased with this mechanic alone, up to and including more competent cultists who must also be covered by Ally, Retainer or certain Merits), and whose support gives you +1 die per dot in the background to Rituals when they are gathered.<br /> <br /> Take Sarah, an Ecstatic idol. She takes 3 dots in Fame and 5 dots in Cult, along with Resources 4. Now all of her Groupies, Entourage, Publicists, Backup Dancers and Vocalists act as her 5 dots in cult. If she performs a Ritual Effect while on stage, then all of this synergises to make magick simple and spectacular. If she performs a &quot;ritual&quot; while her glorified servants are fetching things for her and making themselves useful, it acts like a traditional cult, even though it wouldn't LOOK that way to an outsider. &quot;Oh she makes a big deal of her morning routine. Everything has to be done right, and in the right order. But hell, you can justify being a diva if you've got talent.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now take Eliot, a post-doctorate Etherite. He takes 1 dot in Cult and 5 dots in Laboratory. Now he has the most advanced laboratory most scientists will ever see, and 6 devoted and useful PhD students working in their lab. Easily justified of course; doing advanced research for a respected professor comes with great experience, access to top-notch equipment, and helpful oversight in your dissertation. When the &quot;cult&quot; is in action, Eliot is directing his unenlightened assistants to perform simple procedures which make his acts of magick simpler and more relaxing, adding 1 die to all of the ritual rolls he performs. And if he needs someone to watch the lab while he's away for a day, that's easy enough... just don't expect this PhD student (who is Cult, not Retainer or Ally) to be an expert security guard.<br /> <br /> What's important is that the same fundamental mechanics are being applied differently, with aesthetic and thematic diversity. A good scientist would never call their assistants a cult, much as they wouldn't call what they do &quot;magic&quot;. A pop star might have a &quot;Cult Following&quot;, but they would never put it that way. &quot;People just love me, and who can blame them?&quot; And there really are limitless variations here. All of a dom/dommes' subs. A hypereconomist's devoted employees, interns and assistants. A ruler's advisers. A religious leader's congregation (unless it is more of a cult, in which case we've come full circle).<br /> <br /> All that really matters is that it's a group of sleepers who support the Mage, believe in the rituals they perform on some level (this does not necessitate a belief in Magick!), and/or are able to practically contribute to the ritual. This leaves room for lots of variation and experimentation.<br /> <br /> With all of that said, I'd like to hear people's experiences with the Background, and ideas on different types of cults for different types of Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-08-2018, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T21:10:23-07:00","id":1216891,"title":"","content":"Hah, good examples.<br /> <br /> The 'alternative' word that popped into my head that could have been in the book is simply 'Followers'. I think it fits, especially in this media-driven age, and can apply to all kinds of, as yo say, groupies, students that follow your theories, etc. &quot;Cult / Followers&quot; would have made sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T22:08:00-07:00","id":1216900,"title":"","content":"You could go with fans, since that is short for fanatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T23:36:44-07:00","id":1216912,"title":"","content":"When I think of a non-standard Cult, I think of the teacher and his students from Dead Poets Society. With their &quot;O Captain, My Captain!&quot; and all that. People who believe whole-heartedly in a person. I can totally see a mage of the Society of Ether, New World Order, or Hollow Ones having such a relationship with their students.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:23:06-07:00","id":1216971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult#post1216863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all of that said, I'd like to hear people's experiences with the Background, and ideas on different types of cults for different types of Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an idea that some Mages of the Infernal Nephandi would only recruit as their Acolytes persons that already - without the Nephandi's direct involvement - became infernal cultists, secular satanists, luciferian intellectuals etc. Such persons are seen by those Nephandi as somehow proven and more reliable compared to a person who would be told about and introduced to the concept and the existence of the infernal by a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that the Cult background should be called &quot;Acolytes&quot; or &quot;Believers&quot; .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:35:35-07:00","id":1216976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1216971#post1216971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea that some Mages of the Infernal Nephandi would only recruit as their Acolytes persons that already - without the Nephandi's direct involvement - became infernal cultists, secular satanists, luciferian intellectuals etc. Such persons are seen by those Nephandi as somehow proven and more reliable compared to a person who would be told about and introduced to the concept and the existence of the infernal by a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that the Cult background should be called &quot;Acolytes&quot; or &quot;Believers&quot; .</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I feel Nephandi will employ cults more effectively than normal Mages, due to their truly amoral stance on the importance of individuals. Furthermore, a Marauder with a Sanity Sink could be a god unto their cult. If the Marauder thinks they are the second coming of jesus christ, then their cult is just going to start believing that more and more the more time they spend with them.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, where would that put you in Quiet terms? There are Mages (Quiet 0 in Marauder mechanics) who have &quot;We are all Gods&quot; and &quot;We are not Men&quot; as their Paradigms, so HOW insane is a Mage who thinks they are the Christ? Quiet 1? Because there are some Mages who think (rightly or wrongly) that their father was a fae or a spirit or an angel or a demon. When placed in that perspective, could you even argue that Mages would NOTICE a Marauder who was so sane that their only major delusion was thinking they're Jesus (especially if they have a large cult backing it up). The Mages around them could just think they're faking it, or that they are conventionally insane, or that their Paradigm is clouding their sense of conventional reality (hardly a cardinal sin).<br /> <br /> As for the name... well a Sanctum or a Lab can be called a Dojo or a Grove or a Chamber, and a Cult can be Fans or Fanatics or Acolytes or Believers or Assistants...<br /> <br /> I think that Acolytes / Assistants captures the essence of the Background quite well. Then again I also really like Followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-09-2018, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T07:22:25-07:00","id":1216991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1216976#post1216976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Furthermore, a Marauder with a Sanity Sink could be a god unto their cult. If the Marauder thinks they are the second coming of jesus christ, then their cult is just going to start believing that more and more the more time they spend with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much how a Marauder like Witch-House works, it seems. She has a huge cult following, and is one hell of a sanity sink to boot. Book Of Secrets, page 247/248. She's a really good read.<br /> <br /> Personally it's reasons like the kind of follower she amasses, that I think that the Cult background *really* should go above 5. Yes, the main advantage of a cult is the lessened ritual difficulty, and that might as well stop stacking up at 5, but with a really devoted or even fanatical cult, you can pull of quite a lot more things than just rituals. And while a bunch of people directly aiding you near-blindly might fall under Allies or Backup, none of those two backgrounds can ramp up the numbers as a large Cult could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-09-2018, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T08:18:05-07:00","id":1216997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1216991#post1216991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's pretty much how a Marauder like Witch-House works, it seems. She has a huge cult following, and is one hell of a sanity sink to boot. Book Of Secrets, page 247/248. She's a really good read.<br /> <br /> Personally it's reasons like the kind of follower she amasses, that I think that the Cult background *really* should go above 5. Yes, the main advantage of a cult is the lessened ritual difficulty, and that might as well stop stacking up at 5, but with a really devoted or even fanatical cult, you can pull of quite a lot more things than just rituals. And while a bunch of people directly aiding you near-blindly might fall under Allies or Backup, none of those two backgrounds can ramp up the numbers as a large Cult could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Cult doesn't reduce difficulty, it's actually better than that. Mage is DROWNING in difficulty modifiers. Nothing is going to make you get more successes on a Ritual once you've dropped the Difficulty by 3, except more Dice and Automatic Successes.<br /> <br /> Cult adding dice is actually the best thing it could do, IMO.<br /> <br /> Arete 3, Cult 5, a Coincidental Level 3 effect. Say it's a metal concert where the lead singer (the Mage) is conducting every aspect to kill someone with Correspondence 3 Life 3.<br /> <br /> So it's Difficulty 5, reduced to Difficulty 3 by any of the 100s of modifiers that can do that.<br /> <br /> Now each roll in the Ritual is 8 dice at Difficulty 3. Forget killing one person; you could kill a group of people at this point.<br /> <br /> And it only gets more intense if you have Mages working with the Cult. If your Mage helpers are weaker than you then they can add One Automatic Success each. If you're working equally they can add their dice. If a band of four are all Mages, working together on this death curse, then we could have 17 (3 in Arete each, plus 5 from the Cult) dice per roll, at Difficulty 3.<br /> <br /> And I agree! Cult's mechanical benefits in terms of Dice might cap at 5, but it would be cool if you could push it up to 10 to reflect enormous followings. At 6+, if your Cult has its own community (a compound, a village, a trailer park) then it begins effecting the Reality Zone, generating local reality where your magick is usually coincidental.<br /> <br /> The point of Cult would be quantity over quality in aid. An Ally is a highly competent person who you know well. A cult of 100 is made up of... well sometimes people whose houses aren't entirely in order. The competent members of the cult (your right hand man, the recruiter) could be reflected by Ally of course. But numbers have their advantages! If you are arrested thanks to NWO manipulation, an enormous protest can form within an hour. If you need a bunch of devoted people to simply attend a place en mass, that's always an option. What sane Night Folk will attack someone who is surrounded by 100s of supporters? And it seems likely that in a massive cult, you would find Sorcerers and newly Awakened Mages who will fit into your Paradigm and make a good Apprentice. Participating in magick as a cult member is as good a reason to Awaken as any.<br /> <br /> I read a bit about Witch-House in M20 core, but I didn't know she got more space in BoS! I'll have to take a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-09-2018, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T18:52:41-07:00","id":1217230,"title":"","content":"11twiggins is right. Cult doesn't give breaks on difficulty, it gives extra dice for Ritual work. In that sense, it's entirely necessary that Cult only goes up, in practical terms, to 5 dots. Any more, and we're looking at ridiculous levels of power for comparatively low freebie/experience point investment.<br /> <br /> I'm not one of those folks who shout &quot;ARGLE BLARGLE OVERPOWERED!&quot; at any little thing that sounds OP on paper. But on this score, I'm totally on board with the idea that Cult should be limited to 5 dots. Even at those levels, it's potent enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T23:20:22-07:00","id":1217280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1216997#post1216997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Cult doesn't reduce difficulty,</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217230#post1217230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11twiggins is right. Cult doesn't give breaks on difficulty, it gives extra dice for Ritual work</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an oversimplification, you guys :P More dice, less difficult magic. Although I guess I should have worded it different. Mea Culpa!<br /> <br /> But yes, that's why I said that part of the equation, Bluecho, should probably stop at 5, while it would still make sense for it to go higher for all the other roleplay-related sides and effects of things. And I think the roleplayed effects of a large cult are advantageous enough to actually making it dots instead of saying 'Okay, you have 5 dots, but your cult is actually 200 people in size now'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T00:54:45-07:00","id":1217289,"title":"","content":"Well, a technocratic &quot;cult&quot; could be an enterprise or a business (or a mafia organization). A marauder cult... could be anything. There's so many possibilities and the name shouldn't limit your creativity.<br /> <br /> Also, for cult size, sure it could go beyond anything described in the book, but how many people will you be able to gather for the ritual? Where will you perform a ritual with 200 people and who's gonna keep an eye on all those people doing stuff? There's lot of mistakes waiting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T06:29:39-07:00","id":1217367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1216976#post1216976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly I feel Nephandi will employ cults more effectively than normal Mages, due to their truly amoral stance on the importance of individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you define at least a little this &quot;truly amoral stance on the importance of individuals&quot; that you wrote that the Nephandi Mages have ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:01:25-07:00","id":1217399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217367#post1217367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you define at least a little this &quot;truly amoral stance on the importance of individuals&quot; that you wrote that the Nephandi Mages have ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a key part of the Nephandi philosophy is that people don't matter. A blip on the cosmic radar. To them conventional morality isn't really a worry any more, so I would frame them as amoral over immoral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:03:00-07:00","id":1217400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217230#post1217230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11twiggins is right. Cult doesn't give breaks on difficulty, it gives extra dice for Ritual work. In that sense, it's entirely necessary that Cult only goes up, in practical terms, to 5 dots. Any more, and we're looking at ridiculous levels of power for comparatively low freebie/experience point investment.<br /> <br /> I'm not one of those folks who shout &quot;ARGLE BLARGLE OVERPOWERED!&quot; at any little thing that sounds OP on paper. But on this score, I'm totally on board with the idea that Cult should be limited to 5 dots. Even at those levels, it's potent enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes I agree with Ambrosia that it should cap at 5 dots. But the other aspects could continue to level up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:07:17-07:00","id":1217401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217289#post1217289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a technocratic &quot;cult&quot; could be an enterprise or a business (or a mafia organization). A marauder cult... could be anything. There's so many possibilities and the name shouldn't limit your creativity.<br /> <br /> Also, for cult size, sure it could go beyond anything described in the book, but how many people will you be able to gather for the ritual? Where will you perform a ritual with 200 people and who's gonna keep an eye on all those people doing stuff? There's lot of mistakes waiting to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like any sort of &quot;cult&quot; should have people working with you. So a congregation or a group of assistants makes sense, but framing all the employees of a Venture as a &quot;cult&quot; seems a bit weird. How do you describe their contribution to a Ritual? A hypereconomist would be better off having their PAs, interns and direct subordinates as cult, even if that limits them in terms of numbers.<br /> <br /> As for the logistics of a huge cult, you don't need to use all of them for a ritual. One thing I strongly dislike about the M20 writeup is that it tells you to gather the whole cult to use the Background. Instead it should just give you whatever dice modifier applies to the number present. If you have a 5 dot Cult and only gather 3 dots worth of people, then you get +3 dice. And if you have a 10 dot cult, then you may as well gather 5 dots worth of people for a ritual, as more than 60 or so people draws attention and invites disaster in a single complex ritual. Others can simply observe, sing hymns, watch in awe... if you need them present at all. Remember, cults have hierarchies!<br /> <br /> The &quot;inner circle&quot; of the cult can be your first few dots, and the lower ranks can be the higher dots. A big part of a cult's strength is that people will give years of their life, and huge amounts of money, to climb up the ladder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T20:28:13-07:00","id":1217569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217401#post1217401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like any sort of &quot;cult&quot; should have people working with you. So a congregation or a group of assistants makes sense, but framing all the employees of a Venture as a &quot;cult&quot; seems a bit weird. How do you describe their contribution to a Ritual? A hypereconomist would be better off having their PAs, interns and direct subordinates as cult, even if that limits them in terms of numbers.<br /> <br /> As for the logistics of a huge cult, you don't need to use all of them for a ritual. One thing I strongly dislike about the M20 writeup is that it tells you to gather the whole cult to use the Background. Instead it should just give you whatever dice modifier applies to the number present. If you have a 5 dot Cult and only gather 3 dots worth of people, then you get +3 dice. And if you have a 10 dot cult, then you may as well gather 5 dots worth of people for a ritual, as more than 60 or so people draws attention and invites disaster in a single complex ritual. Others can simply observe, sing hymns, watch in awe... if you need them present at all. Remember, cults have hierarchies!<br /> <br /> The &quot;inner circle&quot; of the cult can be your first few dots, and the lower ranks can be the higher dots. A big part of a cult's strength is that people will give years of their life, and huge amounts of money, to climb up the ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the write-up in M20 precludes that from happening. My reading of the text was that you get the full value of your Cult if everyone is together. It doesn't actually deny you the ability to use smaller numbers of them. I interpret the text as saying exactly what you describe. There is no conflict here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh yes I agree with Ambrosia that it should cap at 5 dots. But the other aspects could continue to level up. </div> </div> </div>On this, we must also disagree. By all means, a character can have a huge a number of people following them as they can manage. This is how religions start.<br /> <br /> However, the point of a Background is indicating a mechanical advantage, which is, in turn, adjudicated by the purchase of same with freebie or experience points. If you have to buy something, those purchases should translate directly into value for the player.<br /> <br /> With those Backgrounds that rise in excess of 5, it's because a character could not only conceivably have that many, but also benefit directly from it. Some people ARE rich enough to command whole industries. The utility of being that wealthy is not up for debate. Cult, however, is explicitly capped in how many followers can contribute to a mage's ritual workings. As such, even if they have an arbitrarily huge number of cultists, they mechanically only have Cult 5 at most. Any more, and you're asking characters to buy dots for a Background that give them no benefit. Not to mention it clogs up the book with descriptions of levels that do nothing.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the problem might be fixed if the write-up simply said &quot;x number of followers, or greater&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T03:27:55-07:00","id":1217611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217399#post1217399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well a key part of the Nephandi philosophy is that people don't matter. A blip on the cosmic radar. To them conventional morality isn't really a worry any more, so I would frame them as amoral over immoral.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is otherwise with the Nephandi - Nephandi Mages can care, and do care, about other persons. For example, wouldn't you agree that the Nephandi seeking out and finding young Widderslaintes, and giving them a place within the Nephandi faction, definitely indicates that other persons do matter to the Nephandi ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T05:22:38-07:00","id":1217630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217611#post1217611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it is otherwise with the Nephandi - Nephandi Mages can care, and do care, about other persons. For example, wouldn't you agree that the Nephandi seeking out and finding young Widderslaintes, and giving them a place within the Nephandi faction, definitely indicates that other persons do matter to the Nephandi ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're confusing &quot;emotional attachment&quot; to &quot;has utility&quot;. Finding Widderslaintes matters to Nephandi because they have utility - more hands on deck makes it easier to further the cause of the Greater Evil. No Fallen, however, would really say they are emotionally attached to a Widderslainte. None would say they &quot;like&quot; the little shits. They are tools to be groomed, used, then thrown away as is convenient.<br /> <br /> However, by that token, I emphatically disagree with the idea that the Nephandi are merely amoral. They are deeply, enthusiastically IMMORAL. Merely being ambivalent to humanity would not motivate Nephandi - collectively - to seek Descent. Merely not caring one way or another what their actions do would not compel them to infiltrate, subvert, and destroy. You'd have a greater range of actions from them if they were merely amoral.<br /> <br /> No, they aren't that. They aren't incidentally bastards. They are focused. They are bastards <i>on purpose</i>, for the simple joy of being bastards. It's a lifestyle and a <i>lower</i> calling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T05:32:16-07:00","id":1217634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217630#post1217630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're confusing &amp;quot;emotional attachment&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;has utility&amp;quot;. Finding Widderslaintes matters to Nephandi because they have utility - more hands on deck makes it easier to further the cause of the Greater Evil. No Fallen, however, would really say they are emotionally attached to a Widderslainte. None would say they &amp;quot;like&amp;quot; the little shits. They are tools to be groomed, used, then thrown away as is convenient.<br /> <br /> However, by that token, I emphatically disagree with the idea that the Nephandi are merely amoral. They are deeply, enthusiastically IMMORAL. Merely being ambivalent to humanity would not motivate Nephandi - collectively - to seek Descent. Merely not caring one way or another what their actions do would not compel them to infiltrate, subvert, and destroy. You'd have a greater range of actions from them if they were merely amoral.<br /> <br /> No, they aren't that. They aren't incidentally bastards. They are focused. They are bastards <i>on purpose</i>, for the simple joy of being bastards. It's a lifestyle and a <i>lower</i> calling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I suppose that they are actively immoral, but their ideology has amoral aspects. The idea that people don't really matter either way is the foundation of their more evil beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T05:34:03-07:00","id":1217635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217569#post1217569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that the write-up in M20 precludes that from happening. My reading of the text was that you get the full value of your Cult if everyone is together. It doesn't actually deny you the ability to use smaller numbers of them. I interpret the text as saying exactly what you describe. There is no conflict here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On this, we must also disagree. By all means, a character can have a huge a number of people following them as they can manage. This is how religions start.<br /> <br /> However, the point of a Background is indicating a mechanical advantage, which is, in turn, adjudicated by the purchase of same with freebie or experience points. If you have to buy something, those purchases should translate directly into value for the player.<br /> <br /> With those Backgrounds that rise in excess of 5, it's because a character could not only conceivably have that many, but also benefit directly from it. Some people ARE rich enough to command whole industries. The utility of being that wealthy is not up for debate. Cult, however, is explicitly capped in how many followers can contribute to a mage's ritual workings. As such, even if they have an arbitrarily huge number of cultists, they mechanically only have Cult 5 at most. Any more, and you're asking characters to buy dots for a Background that give them no benefit. Not to mention it clogs up the book with descriptions of levels that do nothing.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the problem might be fixed if the write-up simply said &quot;x number of followers, or greater&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that Cult 6 would be +5 dice, plus you have a cult of 100 people. There are many mechanical benefits to this. You can get them to do things collectively. 100 devout followers is a mechanical bonus. Same with 400, 1000, 5000...<br /> <br /> For example with 7 dots in cult you might develop your own community somewhere, and form a local reality zone. Or you might monetize your cult. Or you might use them as a Quintessence farm. Or you could have them join certain professions and subvert them for you, as white nationalist &quot;cults&quot; have done with the army and police force in some parts of the US. You get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-11-2018, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T07:33:35-07:00","id":1217663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217630#post1217630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're confusing &quot;emotional attachment&quot; to &quot;has utility&quot;. Finding Widderslaintes matters to Nephandi because they have utility - more hands on deck makes it easier to further the cause of the Greater Evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is because most Nephandi want to save somebody similar to them ; maybe especially so when it is considered that other Mages seem to be prejudiced against Widderslaintes.<br /> Having additional members in the Nephandi faction is a consideration and a factor, as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217630#post1217630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Fallen, however, would really say they are emotionally attached to a Widderslainte. None would say they &quot;like&quot; the little shits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think this is so because you consider Widderslaintes to be very unlikeable in their behaviour ? Or do you think this is so because you think that the Nephandi Mages who aren't Widderslaintes are prejudiced against Widderslaintes ? Or maybe you consider both of these to be true to an extent ?<br /> <br /> I think that the Nephandi Mages who aren't Widderslaintes definitely aren't incapable of being emotionally attatched towards Widderslaintes ( and being friends with them, for example ) . I haven't read anything in any book that suggests that there is any kind of negative prejudice towards Widderslaintes within the Nephandi faction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216863-the-unconventional-cult?p=1217630#post1217630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are tools to be groomed, used, then thrown away as is convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>This in not the case. Nephandi Mages who are Widderslaintes are respected by Nephandi Mages who aren't Widderslaintes, as fellow Nephandi. Widderslainte Nephandi Mages tend towards being leaders of Nephandi groups.<br /> Though it is written that some Barrabi Nephandi see Widderslainte Nephandi as 'effete snobs' .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-11-2018, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}